{
 "experiment": "exp43c arm validity (memorisation control + matched-initialisation B1)",
 "spec": "doc 24 SS5 (qnlp_private_docs/24, commit c6099b0, FROZEN): SS5.2 memorisation control, fixed 64-item L1 subset (first 32 twin pairs by sorted pair_id), grid {lr 0.005, 0.02} x {batch 1, 8}, 2 seeds, <=300 epochs, arm_trainable iff any config reaches train>=0.95; SS5.3 matched-init B1 on the exact frozen L1 Phase-1 grid, <=60 epochs, gate train>=0.8 AND val>=0.7; consequences frozen in SS5.4",
 "platform": "macOS-26.5.2-arm64-arm-64bit",
 "python": "3.12.13",
 "torch": "2.13.0",
 "dataset_sha256": "88cd70ad530356911c17f18d0b42de3edf3c956324513a1455c9548aaef15534",
 "embeddings_sha256": "00c1ecffcaf05b38df082f8a3cbed1d013bddb3e39bc00adf1c2513b4ea674ac",
 "meta": {
  "additive_amendment_A2": "ADDITIVE AMENDMENT: A2 is included in the SS5.2 memorisation control although doc 24 SS5.2 lists {A1, A3, B1, B2, B3}. Reason: F5 (doc 24 SS6) requires every arm entering a comparison to have passed SS5.2, and A2 is the frozen tier-q comparator (doc 23 / doc 24 SS7); without this control A2 could not enter Phase 2 at all. The amendment is additive in the doc 24 SS3 sense: it adds a control our own comparator must pass, which can only make our own claim strictly harder to establish, never easier.",
  "b2_name_augmentation": "Name augmentation (an exp42 training-protocol feature for B2's generalisation) is DISABLED in the memorisation control: the control measures pure fitting/optimisation capacity on a fixed 64-item set, and per-presentation name resampling changes the target being fit. Flagged as an execution resolution; doc 24 SS5.2 does not mention augmentation.",
  "matched_init_scheme": "Execution resolution of SS5.3 'q_pos, q_neg drawn generically': each readout matrix is initialised at a generic SO(4) rotation built as the ordered product of 6 Givens rotations over index pairs (0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(1,2),(1,3),(2,3), each angle uniform on [0, 2pi) via torch.rand -- the real analogue of the A arms' generic uniform-angle init, far from identity, symmetry-breaking, and F4-compliant (torch.rand only). The PARAMETERISATION is unchanged (full 4x4 real matrix, 16 trained entries); only initial values differ. Dressing factors are 2x2 rotations R(theta), theta uniform on [0, 2pi), per the doc's explicit wording. Draws use a fresh generator seeded 51000+seed so the matched draws are a recorded, independent stream; the symmetric-core init is inherited unchanged from B1-as-shipped (torch.rand(2)*2pi, generator seeded with the run seed).",
  "vocab_note": "B2/B3 vocab built over all L1 splits (train+val+test), size 43",
  "memo_subset": {
   "n_items": 64,
   "n_pairs": 32,
   "pair_ids_first_last": [
    "p00001",
    "p00032"
   ],
   "n_yes": 32
  },
  "control_of_the_control": "A1 is the leak sentinel; Lemma 1 pins it to <=0.5 on twins, so it MUST fail SS5.2. If A1 passes, exp43c is INCONCLUSIVE and is acted on in no way (doc 24 SS5.2)."
 },
